WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:03.840
Changes in your diet not
only affect you physically,

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:05.820
physiologically inside,

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:08.580
but also mentally,
how well you think,

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:11.100
psychologically,
how well you feel.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:14.160
But you’ll never know just
how good you can feel

00:00:14.160 --> 00:00:19.020
until you put it to the test
and try eating healthy.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:21.300
Welcome to the
NutritionFacts Podcast.

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:24.360
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:24.600 --> 00:00:28.860
Today we revel in the antioxidant
properties of hibiscus tea,

00:00:28.860 --> 00:00:33.000
which compared to
280 common beverages,

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:36.180
ranks number one for
its antioxidant content—

00:00:36.180 --> 00:00:38.040
even beating out green tea.

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:39.480
In our first story,

00:00:39.480 --> 00:00:41.880
we look at the
results of a randomized,

00:00:41.880 --> 00:00:43.680
double-blind,
placebo-controlled trial

00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:46.129
of hibiscus tea for weight loss.

00:00:46.552 --> 00:00:51.180
Hibiscus tea, also known as roselle or
Jamaica, is enjoyed around the world

00:00:51.180 --> 00:00:55.140
hot or cold for its bright red color
and tart cranberry-like flavor.

00:00:55.140 --> 00:00:57.840
It's the "zing" in Red Zinger tea.

00:00:57.840 --> 00:01:00.060
I talk about its benefits
in the chapter

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:02.160
on high blood pressure
in How Not to Die,

00:01:02.160 --> 00:01:06.420
working as well as some leading
antihypertensive medications

00:01:06.420 --> 00:01:12.120
in head-to-head tests, or
even beating the drugs out.

00:01:12.720 --> 00:01:15.180
Within three hours
of drinking hibiscus tea,

00:01:15.180 --> 00:01:17.580
changes in hundreds
of metabolites can be detected

00:01:17.580 --> 00:01:20.460
in the human bloodstream
with creative names

00:01:20.460 --> 00:01:24.660
like hibiscic acid, or
hibiscin, or hibiscitrin.

00:01:24.660 --> 00:01:27.720
Alterations in human gene
expression at the 3-hour mark

00:01:27.720 --> 00:01:29.940
after drinking it suggest
a downregulation

00:01:29.940 --> 00:01:33.180
of cholesterol synthesis and
an improvement in metabolism.

00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:36.600
But randomized controlled trials
failed to consistently find

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:37.920
cholesterol-lowering benefits.

00:01:37.920 --> 00:01:42.060
An interesting side-effect
popped up, though: weight loss.

00:01:42.780 --> 00:01:45.420
In Mexico, hibiscus tea
has been traditionally used

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:48.720
as a treatment for obesity,
sparking lots of research interest.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:51.480
Computer modeling studies
have suggested that

00:01:51.480 --> 00:01:53.580
certain hibiscus compounds
might bind

00:01:53.580 --> 00:01:56.760
to the fat-digesting enzyme
lipase like a lock-and-key.

00:01:56.760 --> 00:02:00.420
Test tube studies screening
a variety of medicinal plants

00:02:00.420 --> 00:02:02.940
did indeed find hibiscus
inhibited lipase

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:04.200
more than most of the others,

00:02:04.200 --> 00:02:08.880
and hibiscus has been found
to reduce body fat in hamsters,

00:02:08.880 --> 00:02:14.820
mice, and rats,
increasing fecal fat excretion.

00:02:14.820 --> 00:02:20.366
But it wasn't tested in people
until this study published in 2014.

00:02:20.400 --> 00:02:24.900
Spoiler alert: Hibiscus can inhibit
obesity and fat accumulation --

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:28.320
in humans -- and improve fatty liver.

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:31.140
To create a randomized
double-blind trial,

00:02:31.140 --> 00:02:31.920
instead of trying to create

00:02:31.920 --> 00:02:34.260
some artificially colored
and flavored placebo tea,

00:02:34.260 --> 00:02:37.860
they just dried the hibiscus tea
into powder and put it into capsules.

00:02:37.860 --> 00:02:41.400
After 12 weeks, there was
a greater reduction in waistlines

00:02:41.400 --> 00:02:43.440
and percent body fat
in the hibiscus group,

00:02:43.440 --> 00:02:45.720
compared to those who
got placebo capsules.

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:48.720
But the dose they ended up using
was equivalent

00:02:48.720 --> 00:02:51.240
of like nine cups
of hibiscus tea a day.

00:02:51.240 --> 00:02:54.420
I recommend people stick
to no more than a quart a day

00:02:54.420 --> 00:02:57.060
on a regular basis due to
the high manganese content.

00:02:57.060 --> 00:02:59.460
Manganese is an
essential trace mineral,

00:02:59.460 --> 00:03:02.700
but nine cups a day might result
in too much of a good thing.

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:07.980
Finally, in 2018, this study was
published using a reasonable dose --

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:11.940
the equivalent of about a single
12-ounce glass of hibiscus tea a day.

00:03:11.940 --> 00:03:16.620
The complicating factor is that they
also added lemon verbena to the mix.

00:03:16.620 --> 00:03:19.680
That's another herbal tea, better
known for improving recovery

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:21.720
after intense bouts
of strength training,

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:24.900
but there was some promising
in vitro data on effects

00:03:24.900 --> 00:03:27.900
of lemon verbena
on fat cells in a petri dish,

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:29.400
so they tried a combination.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:32.580
It comes out to be about
a cup and a half of hibiscus tea

00:03:32.580 --> 00:03:36.360
and a quarter cup of lemon verbena
tea once a day for two months.

00:03:36.360 --> 00:03:38.820
Both the tea and placebo
groups were fed diets

00:03:38.820 --> 00:03:41.760
containing the same amount
of calories, yet those randomized

00:03:41.760 --> 00:03:44.640
to the tea group lost
significantly more weight --

00:03:44.640 --> 00:03:46.320
five pounds compared
to three pounds.

00:03:46.320 --> 00:03:48.300
That's only an extra
pound or two a month,

00:03:48.300 --> 00:03:50.820
but an extra pound a month
eating the same number of calories.

00:03:50.820 --> 00:03:53.640
That's the advantage of
fat-blocking interventions

00:03:53.640 --> 00:03:55.680
that actually cause you
to lose more calories

00:03:55.680 --> 00:03:58.800
beyond just reducing hunger
and making you feel fuller longer

00:03:58.800 --> 00:04:01.200
in hopes you'll eat fewer
calories in the first place.

00:04:01.800 --> 00:04:04.620
Why not just pop pills
instead of brewing tea?

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:08.400
There's all sorts of herbal extract
supplements on the market,

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:11.100
but that presumes we know
enough to extract out

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:12.780
the right active ingredients.

00:04:12.780 --> 00:04:16.380
For example, it does not appear
to be the red anthocyanin pigments

00:04:16.380 --> 00:04:19.620
in hibiscus, since white varieties
seem to have similar effects.

00:04:19.620 --> 00:04:23.100
When the various compounds
in hibiscus tea are isolated out

00:04:23.100 --> 00:04:26.940
and tested in various combinations,
synergistic effects are found,

00:04:26.940 --> 00:04:30.360
meaning the whole may be
greater than the sum of its parts.

00:04:30.360 --> 00:04:34.620
As with any sour food or beverage,
though (like after eating citrus),

00:04:34.620 --> 00:04:37.680
it's important to wash the
natural acids off your teeth

00:04:37.680 --> 00:04:41.100
by rinsing your mouth out with
water to protect your tooth enamel.

00:04:41.100 --> 00:04:44.820
You also want to wait
at least an hour before brushing,

00:04:44.820 --> 00:04:48.839
so as not to erode your enamel
when it's in a softened state.

00:04:49.260 --> 00:04:50.460
In our next story,

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:53.160
we look at how the blood pressure-
lowering effects of hibiscus tea

00:04:53.160 --> 00:04:55.680
compare to the DASH diet,
a plant-based diet,

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:58.689
and a long-distance
endurance exercise.

00:04:58.920 --> 00:05:01.920
The latest research pitted
hibiscus against obesity,

00:05:01.920 --> 00:05:06.240
giving hibiscus to overweight individuals,
and showed reduced body weight,

00:05:06.240 --> 00:05:09.600
but after 12 weeks on hibiscus
they only lost like 3 pounds,

00:05:09.600 --> 00:05:12.180
and really only one and
a half pounds over placebo—

00:05:12.180 --> 00:05:14.400
clearly no magic fix.

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:18.480
The purported cholesterol-lowering
property of hibiscus tea

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:19.740
had looked a bit
more promising.

00:05:19.740 --> 00:05:22.680
Some older studies suggested
as much as an 8% reduction

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:24.300
drinking two cups
a day for a month,

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:29.040
but when all the studies are put together
the results were pretty much a wash.

00:05:29.640 --> 00:05:32.940
This may be because only about
50% of people respond at all

00:05:32.940 --> 00:05:36.000
to drinking the equivalent of
between 2 to 5 cups a day,

00:05:36.000 --> 00:05:41.460
though those that do respond may get a
respectable 12 or so percent drop in cholesterol,

00:05:41.460 --> 00:05:44.820
but nothing like the
30% drop one can get

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:48.060
within weeks of eating a
healthy enough plant-based diet.

00:05:49.140 --> 00:05:52.620
High blood pressure is where
hibiscus may really shine,

00:05:52.620 --> 00:05:56.040
a disease affecting a billion
people, killing millions.

00:05:56.040 --> 00:06:00.180
Up until 2010, there wasn’t sufficient
high quality research out there

00:06:00.180 --> 00:06:02.340
to support the use of
hibiscus tea to treat it,

00:06:02.340 --> 00:06:05.820
but there are now randomized double-blind,
placebo-controlled studies

00:06:05.820 --> 00:06:10.260
where hibiscus tea is compared to
artificially colored and flavored water

00:06:10.260 --> 00:06:14.760
that looks and tastes like hibiscus tea,
and the tea did significantly better.

00:06:15.540 --> 00:06:18.060
We’re still not
sure why it works,

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:21.000
but hibiscus does appear to
boost nitric oxide production,

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:24.240
which could help our arteries
relax and dilate better.

00:06:24.240 --> 00:06:28.800
Regardless, an updated review acknowledged
that the daily consumption of hibiscus tea

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:32.100
may indeed significantly lower blood
pressures in people with hypertension,

00:06:32.100 --> 00:06:34.080
but by how much?

00:06:35.040 --> 00:06:38.940
How does this drop in blood pressure
compare to other interventions?

00:06:38.940 --> 00:06:43.140
Well, the premier clinical trial when
it comes to comprehensive lifestyle modification

00:06:43.140 --> 00:06:46.860
for blood pressure control is
the Premier Clinical Trial.

00:06:47.400 --> 00:06:50.820
Realizing that 9 out of 10 Americans
are going to develop hypertension,

00:06:50.820 --> 00:06:55.680
they randomized 800 men and women with
high blood pressure into one of three groups.

00:06:56.220 --> 00:06:59.220
One was the control group,
the so-called advice only group,

00:06:59.220 --> 00:07:02.580
where patients were just told
to lose weight, cut down on salt,

00:07:02.580 --> 00:07:03.840
increase exercise and eat healthier...
here’s a brochure.

00:07:03.840 --> 00:07:06.540
In the two behavioral intervention
groups they got serious.

00:07:06.540 --> 00:07:09.600
18 face-to-face sessions,
groups meetings, food diaries,

00:07:09.600 --> 00:07:12.120
monitored physical activity,
calorie and sodium intake.

00:07:12.120 --> 00:07:15.000
Now, one intervention group
just concentrated on exercise

00:07:15.000 --> 00:07:17.760
and the other one included
exercise and diet.

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:20.880
They pushed the DASH diet,
high in fruits, and vegetables,

00:07:20.880 --> 00:07:23.400
and low in full-fat
dairy products and meat.

00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:29.880
And in six months achieved a 4.3 point
drop in systolic blood pressure,

00:07:29.880 --> 00:07:33.840
compared to the control, slightly better than
the lifestyle intervention without the diet.

00:07:34.440 --> 00:07:37.380
Now, a few points might
not sound like a lot—

00:07:37.380 --> 00:07:43.080
that’s like someone going from a blood pressure
of 150 over 90 to a blood pressure of 146 over 90—

00:07:43.860 --> 00:07:48.360
but on a population scale a 5 point
drop in the total number

00:07:48.360 --> 00:07:52.020
could result in a
14% fewer stroke deaths,

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:57.000
9% fewer fatal heart attacks,
and 7% fewer deaths every year overall.

00:07:57.780 --> 00:08:03.240
But a cup of hibiscus tea with each meal didn’t
just lower blood pressure by 3, 4 or 5 points

00:08:03.240 --> 00:08:09.300
but by 7 points, 129 down to 122.

00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:13.920
And in fact tested head-to-head against a
leading blood-pressure drug, called Captopril,

00:08:13.920 --> 00:08:16.740
two cups of strong
hibiscus tea every morning,

00:08:16.740 --> 00:08:19.500
using a total of 5 tea bags
for those 2 cups,

00:08:19.500 --> 00:08:21.690
was as effective in
lowering blood pressure

00:08:21.690 --> 00:08:25.560
as a starting dose of 25 mg of
Captopril taken twice a day.

00:08:25.560 --> 00:08:29.400
So as good as drugs,
without the drug side-effects,

00:08:29.400 --> 00:08:31.680
and better than
diet and exercise?

00:08:32.640 --> 00:08:36.900
Well, the lifestyle interventions
were pretty whimpy.

00:08:36.900 --> 00:08:40.440
As public health experts noted,
the Premier study

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:44.160
was only asking for 30 minutes
of exercise a day,

00:08:44.160 --> 00:08:48.240
whereas the World Health Organization
is more like an hour a day minimum.

00:08:48.840 --> 00:08:53.760
And diet-wise, the lower
the animal fat intake,

00:08:53.760 --> 00:08:58.140
and the more plant sources of protein
the Premier participants were eating,

00:08:58.140 --> 00:08:59.580
the better the diet
appeared to work,

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:04.140
which may explain why vegetarian diets
appear to work even better,

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:08.520
and the more plant-based the lower
the prevalence of hypertension.

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:13.020
On the DASH diet, they were
told to cut down on meat,

00:09:13.020 --> 00:09:14.400
but were still eating
meat every day,

00:09:14.400 --> 00:09:17.940
so would qualify as the non-vegetarians
here in the Adventist 2 study,

00:09:17.940 --> 00:09:20.040
which looked at
89,000 Californians

00:09:20.040 --> 00:09:23.280
and found that those who instead only
ate meat on more like a weekly basis

00:09:23.280 --> 00:09:25.680
had 23% lower rates
of high blood pressure.

00:09:25.680 --> 00:09:29.460
Cut out all meat except fish
and the rate is 38% lower.

00:09:29.460 --> 00:09:33.180
Cut out all meat period—the vegetarians
have less than half the rate

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:36.420
and the vegans—cutting out
all animal protein and fat—

00:09:36.420 --> 00:09:40.620
appeared to have thrown three quarters of their
risk of this major killer out the window.

00:09:42.060 --> 00:09:46.080
One sees the same kind of step-wise
drop in diabetes rates

00:09:46.080 --> 00:09:50.940
as one’s diet gets more and more plant-based
and a drop in excess body weight

00:09:50.940 --> 00:09:53.400
such that only those eating completely&nbsp;

00:09:53.400 --> 00:09:55.920
plant-based diets fell into&nbsp;
the ideal weight category.

00:09:56.520 --> 00:10:00.480
But could that be why those eating
plant-based have such great blood pressure?

00:10:00.480 --> 00:10:03.360
Maybe it’s just because they’re
so skinny on average.

00:10:03.360 --> 00:10:06.240
I’ve shown previously how those
eating plant based diets

00:10:06.240 --> 00:10:09.540
have just a fraction of the diabetes
risk even at the same weight,

00:10:09.540 --> 00:10:11.700
even after controlling for BMI.

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:14.100
But what about hypertension?

00:10:14.100 --> 00:10:18.540
The average American has
what’s called prehypertension,

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:21.660
which means the top number of your blood
pressure is between 120 and 139.

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:24.360
Not yet hypertension,
which starts at 140,

00:10:24.360 --> 00:10:27.060
but it means we may
be well on our way.

00:10:27.660 --> 00:10:31.260
Compare that to the blood pressure of those
eating whole food plant-based diets.

00:10:31.260 --> 00:10:36.900
Not 3 points lower, 4 points lower, or even
7 points lower, but 28 points lower.

00:10:37.860 --> 00:10:41.460
Now, but the group here eating the
standard American diet was, on average,

00:10:41.460 --> 00:10:46.500
overweight with a BMI over 26,
still better than most Americans,

00:10:47.280 --> 00:10:53.640
but while the vegans were a trim 21
over here—that's 36 pounds lighter.

00:10:54.180 --> 00:10:58.020
So maybe the only reason those eating meat,
eggs, dairy, and processed junk

00:10:58.020 --> 00:11:00.840
had such higher blood pressure
was because they were overweight,

00:11:00.840 --> 00:11:03.480
maybe the diet per se
had nothing to do with it.

00:11:03.480 --> 00:11:05.760
To solve that riddle we
would have to find a group

00:11:05.760 --> 00:11:09.120
still eating the standard American diet
but as slim as a vegan.

00:11:09.120 --> 00:11:13.740
To find a group that fit and trim, they
had to use long-distance endurance athletes,

00:11:13.740 --> 00:11:16.080
who ate the same
crappy American diet —

00:11:16.080 --> 00:11:20.160
but ran an average of 48 miles
a week for 21 years.

00:11:20.880 --> 00:11:23.700
They ran almost two marathons
a week for 20 years.

00:11:24.360 --> 00:11:30.480
So, if you do that, you know, anyone can be
slim as a vegan—no matter what they eat.

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:34.920
So it appears if you run about
a thousand miles every year

00:11:34.920 --> 00:11:38.611
you can start to rival
some couch potato vegans.

00:11:38.611 --> 00:11:43.820
Doesn’t mean you can’t do both,
but it may be easier to just eat plants.

00:11:44.280 --> 00:11:45.180
Finally today,

00:11:45.180 --> 00:11:48.780
the impressive manganese
content of hibiscus tea

00:11:48.780 --> 00:11:52.528
may be the limiting factor for
safe daily levels of consumption.

00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:55.980
Over the counter antacids are
probably the most important source

00:11:55.980 --> 00:11:58.380
for human aluminum exposure
in terms of dose.

00:11:58.380 --> 00:12:01.920
Maalox, for example, taken as directed,
can exceed the daily safety limit

00:12:01.920 --> 00:12:03.240
more than 100-fold,

00:12:03.240 --> 00:12:06.360
and nowhere on the
label does it say not take

00:12:06.360 --> 00:12:08.400
with acidic beverages
such as fruit juice.

00:12:08.400 --> 00:12:11.520
Washing an antacid down with
orange juice, for example,

00:12:11.520 --> 00:12:13.620
can increase aluminum
absorption 8-fold,

00:12:13.620 --> 00:12:15.360
and citric acid
was worse—

00:12:15.360 --> 00:12:18.300
the acid found naturally
concentrated in lemon and limes.

00:12:18.900 --> 00:12:21.780
Just as sour fruits can enhance
the absorption of iron,

00:12:21.780 --> 00:12:24.300
which is a good thing,
through the same mechanism

00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:26.520
they may enhance the
absorption of aluminum,

00:12:26.520 --> 00:12:30.120
raising the question what happens
when one adds lemon juice to tea?

00:12:30.780 --> 00:12:33.120
Previously, I concluded that the
amount of aluminum in tea

00:12:33.120 --> 00:12:35.700
is not a problem for most people
because it’s not very absorbable,

00:12:35.700 --> 00:12:37.380
but what if you
add lemon?

00:12:38.220 --> 00:12:40.740
No difference between
tea with lemon,

00:12:40.740 --> 00:12:42.840
tea without lemon,
or no tea at all

00:12:42.840 --> 00:12:45.000
in terms of the amount of
aluminum in the bloodstream,

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:48.000
suggesting that tea drinking does
not significantly contribute

00:12:48.000 --> 00:12:51.300
to aluminum actually getting inside
the body-lemon juice or not.

00:12:52.020 --> 00:12:54.960
Now, they’re talking about black tea,
green tea, white tea, oolong tea.

00:12:54.960 --> 00:12:57.480
What about the red zinger
herbal tea, hibiscus?

00:12:57.480 --> 00:13:01.920
The reason it’s called sour tea is because it
has natural acids in it like citric acid—

00:13:01.920 --> 00:13:04.380
might that boost the absorption
of any of its aluminum?

00:13:05.160 --> 00:13:09.000
Well, a greater percentage of aluminum gets
from the hibiscus into the tea water,

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:11.700
but there’s less
aluminum overall.

00:13:11.700 --> 00:13:15.480
The question is does the aluminum then
get from the tea water into our body?

00:13:15.480 --> 00:13:20.040
We don’t have that data so to be on the
safe side we should assume the worst -

00:13:20.040 --> 00:13:23.400
that hibiscus tea aluminum, unlike
green and black tea aluminum,

00:13:23.400 --> 00:13:24.660
is completely absorbable.

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:28.620
In that case, based on this data and the
World Health Organization weekly safety limit

00:13:28.620 --> 00:13:33.600
we may not want to drink more than
like 15 cups of hibiscus tea a day

00:13:33.600 --> 00:13:36.000
That’s based on someone
who’s about 150 pounds.

00:13:36.960 --> 00:13:39.840
So if you have a 75 pound
10-year-old,

00:13:39.840 --> 00:13:44.160
a half gallon of tea a day may
be theoretically too much.

00:13:44.160 --> 00:13:46.620
And more extensive testing
more recently suggests

00:13:46.620 --> 00:13:48.720
levels may be as high
as twice as much,

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:51.720
so no more than about two quarts
a day for adults,

00:13:51.720 --> 00:13:55.680
or a quart a day for kids
every day or pregnant women.

00:13:56.280 --> 00:14:00.420
And hibiscus tea should be completely
avoided by infants under 6 months—

00:14:00.420 --> 00:14:03.840
who should only be getting
breast milk anyway—

00:14:03.840 --> 00:14:08.280
as well as kids with kidney failure,
who can’t efficiently excrete it.

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:11.400
The study also raised concern
about the impressive

00:14:11.400 --> 00:14:13.740
manganese level
in hibiscus tea.

00:14:13.740 --> 00:14:16.200
Manganese is an essential
trace mineral,

00:14:16.200 --> 00:14:19.080
a vital component of some of our
most important antioxidant enzymes,

00:14:19.080 --> 00:14:22.080
but we probably only need
2 to 5 milligrams a day,

00:14:22.080 --> 00:14:27.180
and 4 cups of hibiscus tea can have
as much as 17, averaging about 10.

00:14:27.180 --> 00:14:27.900
Is that a problem?

00:14:27.900 --> 00:14:31.800
Well, women given 15 a day
for 4 months, if anything,

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:36.720
only saw an improvement in their
anti-inflammatory, anti-oxidant enzyme activity.

00:14:36.720 --> 00:14:42.420
This study using 20 a day similarly
showed no adverse short-term effects,

00:14:42.420 --> 00:14:46.500
and importantly showed that the retention
of dietary manganese is regulated.

00:14:46.500 --> 00:14:49.200
Our body’s not stupid;
if we take too much in,

00:14:49.200 --> 00:14:53.160
our body decreases the absorption,
and increases the excretion.

00:14:53.160 --> 00:14:57.210
So, even though tea drinkers may
drink 10 times more manganese,

00:14:57.210 --> 00:15:02.280
you get 10 times more a day,
10 or 20 milligrams a day,

00:15:02.280 --> 00:15:06.240
the levels in their blood
is essentially identical.

00:15:06.780 --> 00:15:11.520
So, there is little evidence that
dietary manganese poses a risk.

00:15:11.520 --> 00:15:15.180
That was regular tea, though, we don’t
know about the absorption from hibiscus,

00:15:15.180 --> 00:15:16.740
so to err on the side of
caution we should probably

00:15:16.740 --> 00:15:19.620
not routinely exceed the reference
dose of 10 mg per day,

00:15:19.620 --> 00:15:22.980
so that’s only about a
quart a day for adults,

00:15:22.980 --> 00:15:24.660
a half quart for
a 75 pound child.

00:15:24.660 --> 00:15:28.320
So, that’s actually changed
my family's consumption.

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:32.700
Given the benefits of the stuff, I was using
it as a substitute for drinking water,

00:15:32.700 --> 00:15:37.260
so like 2 liters a day, and I was
blending the hibiscus petals in,

00:15:37.260 --> 00:15:40.140
not throwing them away, effectively
doubling aluminum content,

00:15:40.140 --> 00:15:42.900
and increasing manganese
concentrations by about 30%.

00:15:42.900 --> 00:15:50.843
So, given this data I’ve cut back to no more than
about a quart of filtered hibiscus tea a day.

